#: ../../source/docs/sub-hardware.rst:7
#: abd681273cb246548588604a1bc4c051
msgid "While the Sub firmware is currently being generalized to allow more flexibility, such as RC control, re-arrangement of outputs and inputs, etc., current code is targeted for a specific ROV configuration with the following hardware setup:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sub-hardware.rst:10
#: 80c9b4edde244814b11555caee38f2a3
msgid "Control is via a surface tether from a ground control station via MAVLink commands to the Sub's autopilot telemetry port, usually employing a joystick and multiple buttons for mode changes and peripheral hardware control. Control functions and autopilot outputs for thrusters and peripheral hardware have specific defaults (see :ref:`Sub defaults <sub-defaults>` below)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sub-hardware.rst:11
#: 9e511088f92d46ba9e163f0c07bdbe1c
msgid "A depth sensor (underwater barometer) is required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sub-hardware.rst:12
#: 0ba4da3acead495e8028d1f40de598f4
msgid "Frame configuration is defaulted to Vectored with 6 thrusters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sub-hardware.rst:17
#: 94c8af4785994958839d4409fe35167f
msgid "Sub Defaults"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sub-hardware.rst:18
#: b2dd6a2990dc4080b0bf89acf48938c9
msgid "Default :ref:`frame type <FRAME_TYPE>` is VECTORED"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sub-hardware.rst:19
#: 125833eed24a45c7b948fe314ff17c30
msgid "Radio control is disabled via :ref:`RC_PROTOCOLS<RC_PROTOCOLS>` = 0 and :ref:`FLTMODE_CH<FLTMODE_CH>` = 0. Water absorbs radio waves, so RC is generally impractical unless the vehicle is at the surface, or the signal is converted to some other medium in between (e.g. using a tether cable, or acoustic modems)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sub-hardware.rst:22
#: f6a40cd87cb34673b7074d5a3b344994
msgid "MAVLink Overrides"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sub-hardware.rst:23
#: 056cc04c7eab4e00b9d729d7dac65899
msgid "ArduPilot vehicles normally use radio control (RC) to provide pilot directional control. Since Sub has RC disabled by default, it instead provides directional control with `MAVLink RC overrides <https://mavlink.io/en/services/manual_control.html#alternatives>`__, and the channel mapping is fixed:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sub-hardware.rst:25
#: 8cb9095e11d34b43a46c588ee2255e8d
